No existing OpenRouter or swarm code in the repo. Here's the design from scratch.

---

## OpenRouter Model Swarm — Design Matrix

### Model Tiers

| Tier | Models | Strengths | Cost Range |
|------|--------|-----------|------------|
| **Orchestrator** | Claude Opus 4.6, GPT-5.4 | Planning, decomposition, quality gates | $15-30/M tokens |
| **Workhorse** | Claude Sonnet 4.6, GPT-5.4-mini, Gemini 3.1 Pro | Balanced quality/speed for bulk work | $3-10/M tokens |
| **Fast** | Claude Haiku 4.5, GPT-5.4-nano, Gemini Flash | Iteration, validation, simple transforms | $0.25-1/M tokens |
| **Specialist** | Codex (code), Qwen 3 (multilingual), DeepSeek R1 (math/reasoning) | Domain-specific excellence | Varies |

### Task → Swarm Mapping

**Website Build:**
| Agent | Model | Role |
|-------|-------|------|
| Architect | Opus 4.6 | Decompose requirements, define component tree |
| Frontend | Sonnet 4.6 | React/Next.js components |
| Backend | Codex or Sonnet 4.6 | API routes, DB schema |
| Design | GPT-5.4 | CSS/styling, visual decisions |
| QA | Haiku 4.5 | Lint, type-check, test generation |
| Reviewer | Opus 4.6 | Final quality gate |

**Legal Research:**
| Agent | Model | Role |
|-------|-------|------|
| Researcher | GPT-5.4 (128k) | Long document analysis |
| Legal Analyst | Opus 4.6 | Reasoning over precedent |
| Citation Validator | Haiku 4.5 | Verify references exist |
| Summarizer | Sonnet 4.6 | Client-facing output |

**Marketing:**
| Agent | Model | Role |
|-------|-------|------|
| Copywriter | GPT-5.4 | Creative generation |
| SEO Analyst | Haiku 4.5 | Keyword density, structure check |
| Brand Reviewer | Opus 4.6 | Tone/voice consistency gate |

### Routing Logic

```
Pearl receives task
  → Classify: {complexity, domain, latency_requirement, budget}
  → Select tier:
      complexity=high OR quality_critical → Orchestrator tier
      standard_work → Workhorse tier
      validation/simple_transform → Fast tier
      domain_specific → Specialist tier
  → Fallback chain: Primary → Same-tier alt → Tier-up
  → Rate limit: per-model token bucket (OpenRouter handles this)
```

### Code — OpenRouter Multi-Model Orchestrator

```typescript
// packages/swarm/src/openrouter-swarm.ts

interface ModelConfig {
  id: string;
  tier: 'orchestrator' | 'workhorse' | 'fast' | 'specialist';
  costPer1kInput: number;
  costPer1kOutput: number;
  maxContext: number;
  fallback?: string;
}

const MODEL_REGISTRY: Record<string, ModelConfig> = {
  'anthropic/claude-opus-4-6': {
    id: 'anthropic/claude-opus-4-6',
    tier: 'orchestrator',
    costPer1kInput: 0.015,
    costPer1kOutput: 0.075,
    maxContext: 200000,
    fallback: 'openai/gpt-5.4',
  },
  'anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6': {
    id: 'anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6',
    tier: 'workhorse',
    costPer1kInput: 0.003,
    costPer1kOutput: 0.015,
    maxContext: 200000,
    fallback: 'google/gemini-3.1-pro',
  },
  'anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5': {
    id: 'anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5',
    tier: 'fast',
    costPer1kInput: 0.0008,
    costPer1kOutput: 0.004,
    maxContext: 200000,
    fallback: 'openai/gpt-5.4-nano',
  },
};

interface SwarmTask {
  id: string;
  type: string;
  prompt: string;
  requiredTier: ModelConfig['tier'];
  parentTaskId?: string;
  budget?: number; // max cost in dollars
}

interface SwarmResult {
  taskId: string;
  model: string;
  output: string;
  cost: number;
  latencyMs: number;
}

class OpenRouterSwarm {
  private apiKey: string;
  private baseUrl = 'https://openrouter.ai/api/v1';
  private totalSpend = 0;
  private budgetLimit: number;

  constructor(apiKey: string, budgetLimit = 10.0) {
    this.apiKey = apiKey;
    this.budgetLimit = budgetLimit;
  }

  /** Select best model for a task tier, respecting budget */
  private selectModel(tier: ModelConfig['tier']): ModelConfig {
    const candidates = Object.values(MODEL_REGISTRY).filter(
      (m) => m.tier === tier
    );
    // Sort by cost (cheapest first if budget is tight)
    const budgetRemaining = this.budgetLimit - this.totalSpend;
    if (budgetRemaining < 1.0) {
      candidates.sort((a, b) => a.costPer1kInput - b.costPer1kInput);
    }
    return candidates[0];
  }

  /** Execute a single task against OpenRouter */
  async executeTask(task: SwarmTask): Promise<SwarmResult> {
    const model = this.selectModel(task.requiredTier);
    const start = Date.now();

    try {
      const response = await fetch(`${this.baseUrl}/chat/completions`, {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: {
          Authorization: `Bearer ${this.apiKey}`,
          'Content-Type': 'application/json',
          'X-Title': 'Nia-Swarm',
        },
        body: JSON.stringify({
          model: model.id,
          messages: [{ role: 'user', content: task.prompt }],
          max_tokens: 4096,
        }),
      });

      if (!response.ok) {
        // Fallback to alternate model
        if (model.fallback) {
          return this.executeTask({
            ...task,
            requiredTier: MODEL_REGISTRY[model.fallback]?.tier ?? 'workhorse',
          });
        }
        throw new Error(`OpenRouter ${response.status}: ${await response.text()}`);
      }

      const data = await response.json();
      const usage = data.usage ?? { prompt_tokens: 0, completion_tokens: 0 };
      const cost =
        (usage.prompt_tokens / 1000) * model.costPer1kInput +
        (usage.completion_tokens / 1000) * model.costPer1kOutput;

      this.totalSpend += cost;

      return {
        taskId: task.id,
        model: model.id,
        output: data.choices[0].message.content,
        cost,
        latencyMs: Date.now() - start,
      };
    } catch (err) {
      if (model.fallback) {
        return this.executeTask({
          ...task,
          requiredTier: MODEL_REGISTRY[model.fallback]?.tier ?? 'workhorse',
        });
      }
      throw err;
    }
  }

  /** Run multiple tasks in parallel */
  async executeSwarm(tasks: SwarmTask[]): Promise<SwarmResult[]> {
    // Group independent tasks for parallel execution
    const independent = tasks.filter((t) => !t.parentTaskId);
    const dependent = tasks.filter((t) => t.parentTaskId);

    // Execute independent tasks in parallel
    const results = await Promise.all(
      independent.map((task) => this.executeTask(task))
    );

    // Execute dependent tasks sequentially (could optimize with DAG)
    for (const task of dependent) {
      const parentResult = results.find((r) => r.taskId === task.parentTaskId);
      if (parentResult) {
        task.prompt = `Context from previous step:\n${parentResult.output}\n\n${task.prompt}`;
      }
      results.push(await this.executeTask(task));
    }

    return results;
  }

  getSpendReport() {
    return {
      totalSpend: this.totalSpend,
      budgetRemaining: this.budgetLimit - this.totalSpend,
    };
  }
}

export { OpenRouterSwarm, type SwarmTask, type SwarmResult, MODEL_REGISTRY };
```

### Usage — Website Build Swarm

```typescript
const swarm = new OpenRouterSwarm(process.env.OPENROUTER_API_KEY!, 5.0);

const results = await swarm.executeSwarm([
  {
    id: 'arch',
    type: 'architecture',
    requiredTier: 'orchestrator',
    prompt: 'Decompose this website into components: [spec]',
  },
  {
    id: 'frontend',
    type: 'code',
    requiredTier: 'workhorse',
    parentTaskId: 'arch',
    prompt: 'Build React components for: [component tree]',
  },
  {
    id: 'backend',
    type: 'code',
    requiredTier: 'workhorse',
    parentTaskId: 'arch',
    prompt: 'Build API routes for: [endpoints]',
  },
  {
    id: 'qa',
    type: 'validation',
    requiredTier: 'fast',
    parentTaskId: 'frontend',
    prompt: 'Review this code for bugs and type errors: [code]',
  },
]);

console.log(swarm.getSpendReport());
```

### Cost Estimates Per Task Type

| Task | Models Used | Est. Tokens | Est. Cost |
|------|------------|-------------|-----------|
| Website (simple) | Opus + 2x Sonnet + Haiku | ~150k | $1.50-3.00 |
| Website (complex) | Opus + 4x Sonnet + 2x ...
